- {'file': 'tests/orca-mac-keybindings.sh', 'line': 61, 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': "Hyprland->Orca chord mapping exists twice (generator MODS/KEYS and the test's jq map)", 'reason': "Deliberate: the test is an independent oracle for the generator's filter; sharing the generator's mapping would make case 2 agree with any bug in it. Mutation check confirmed case 2 fails when the filter is removed."}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings-merge.js', 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': "keybindings.json and sidecar are two writes; a failure between them leaves a generated key classed as the UI's", 'reason': 'Needs the second of two tiny same-dir writes to fail (ENOSPC); either order has the window, and the cost is one key frozen until edited in the UI. Not worth a journal.'}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings-merge.js', 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': "Withdrawal can re-expose an action's Linux default, which may clash with a second UI key; only generated ids are withdrawn", 'reason': 'Needs two UI keys deliberately aimed at a generated chord and its Ctrl default; Orca then reports it in its own diagnostics. Contrived; the comment was narrowed to what the loop guarantees.'}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings.js', 'line': 33, 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': "taken/isTaken compares canonical strings with /1$/ digit surgery instead of Orca's conflict identities", 'reason': 'Correct as written: Mod is rewritten away before comparison and the canonical digit binding ends in 1 (canonicalizeDigitIndexBinding); cases 11/13 pin the family behaviour. The new shadow pass already uses keybindingConflictIdentities.'}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings-merge.js', 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': "Creating keybindings.json when absent pre-empts Orca's one-time legacy settings migration (LHn)", 'reason': "Only reachable on a box with pre-file legacy overrides and no keybindings.json; every host here already has the file or never ran an Orca old enough to store them. Detecting legacy settings means reading Orca's settings store, out of scope."}

- {'file': 'tests/orca-mac-keybindings.sh', 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': 'No case for a non-object JSON file or legacy root-shape common section', 'reason': 'Non-object shares the unparseable branch case 6 pins; legacy root shape is a hand-written format Orca never writes. Probed manually by the round-3 error-handling reviewer (all exit 0, correct).'}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings-merge.js', 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': 'A hand-written common (.keybindings) value on a generated action is shadowed by the generated platforms.linux value', 'reason': "Orca's own UI writer (zHn) only ever writes the platform section; common is reachable by hand edits alone, and a hand-editor can put the same value under platforms.linux, which the merge does respect."}

- {'file': 'tests/orca-mac-keybindings.sh', 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': 'No case pins the effective-map update after a withdrawal (cascade where a restored default clashes with another generated key)', 'reason': 'The shadow pass in the generator already prevents generated chords from landing on fallback defaults at build time; a merge-time cascade needs a UI clash that re-exposes a default colliding with a second generated key -- the same contrived shape as the earlier deferred cascade nit.'}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings-merge.js', 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': 'A never-claimed UI value exactly equal to the generated value is recorded as claimed, so a later generation dropping that key deletes it', 'reason': "Needs a pre-existing UI value byte-identical to the Mac chord; the user then already has that chord, and losing it only when a later generation drops the action leaves them on Orca's default. A sentinel state in the sidecar costs more format complexity than the edge is worth."}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings-merge.js', 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': "A settings save by a running Orca between the merge's read and rename is overwritten", 'reason': 'Millisecond window during activation, only if the user saves a shortcut in that instant; the next switch merges again and Orca re-reads before each save. An mtime re-check would narrow, not close, the race.'}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings.js', 'line': 91, 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': 'Shadow pass compares conflict identities across all scopes, broader than the cross-scope dispatch its comment justifies', 'reason': "Errs safe: an over-broad match only leaves an action on Orca's own Linux default and names it in the build log; it never ships a dead key. Orca's cross-scope dispatch order (window-shortcut-policy.js) is code, not exported data, so a precise restriction would hard-code a copy of it that drifts on bumps."}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings.js', 'line': 106, 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': 'No test pins the build-time findKeybindingConflicts throw', 'reason': "A fixture needs a pair of Orca actions whose Mac defaults collide on Linux; none exists in 1.4.238, and fabricating one means stubbing Orca's module, testing the stub rather than the guard. The guard is three lines over Orca's own checker."}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings.js', 'line': 35, 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': 'NO_CHORD omits keysyms Orca can never express (Home, End, Caps_Lock, KP_Enter, KP_1..), so adding such a Hyprland bind fails the build', 'reason': 'Deliberate fail-closed (b1909c92): none is bound today, and the error names the one-line fix (add to NO_CHORD). Pre-listing keys from probing one Orca version would go stale the moment Orca learns a name.'}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings.js', 'line': 60, 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': "Orca's UI hint string ('Use a shortcut like Ctrl+Shift+P') becomes the build error's detail", 'reason': 'Cosmetic; the message already names the bind and the fix. Changing it now would reset two clean rounds for a log string.'}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings-merge.js', 'line': 164, 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': 'Sidecar ...owned spread is near-dead since per-key ownership, and its comment describes the earlier model', 'reason': 'Comment-only plus the already-deferred equal-value case; editing it would reset the clean-round count for no observable change. Follow-up: drop the spread and refresh the comment.'}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings-merge.js', 'line': 81, 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': 'Bad-sidecar abort comment is stale under per-key ownership, and case 14 no longer pins the guard', 'reason': 'The guard still keeps stale generated keys removable; only its stated rationale is outdated. Follow-up with the comment refresh above.'}

- {'file': 'nix/orca-mac-keybindings.js', 'line': 33, 'severity': 'nit', 'summary': 'Numpad binds take only Numpad* chords, not the main-row punctuation chords the same press also matches', 'reason': 'Leaving those chords free ships no dead key (the main-row press still reaches Orca), and no numpad binds exist.'}

